    {
      "claim_id": "hierarchical/Q1.2/019",
      "text": "Hexane and ethanol form a highly non-ideal mixture. The **positive excess molar enthalpy** (≈ 0.56 kJ/mol near x = 0.5) reflects the endothermic disruption of ethanol's hydrogen-bond network upon dilution with the non-polar alkane. The **positive excess molar volume** (≈ 4.1×10⁻⁷ m³/mol ≈ 0.41 cm³/mol) indicates a volume expansion on mixing, consistent with weaker unlike (ethanol–hexane) interactions compared to the self-associations in pure ethanol. Both excess properties exhibit maxima near the equimolar region, which is characteristic of systems with strong hydrogen-bonding asymmetry.",
